          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00354:alt:fig-00005-alt",
              "text": "A carbonyl compound reacts with water having two lone pairs on oxygen to form an intermediate that leads to carbamic acid. This leads to two products, amine and carbon dioxide."
